    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0832" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1162/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-15T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                                1926—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>64. Your telegram number 126, March 13, 5 p.m. Department approves the
                    instructions to Canton as given in your paragraphs 2, 3, and 4.<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d564-f1"/> In the judgment of the Department, military force should
                    be employed only as a last resort and only if considered to be absolutely
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d564-f1" n="91" xml:id="d564-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently refers to last three paragraphs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
